Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:01:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] PS3 login (Ps3ForMmpRequest) for Black Ops II; bind
 auth/lobby to any address

The game puts a random 24-byte key in its PSN ticket's cookie; the reply
ticket is 3DES-encrypted with it and padded to the 152 bytes BO2 reads.
Tickets are parsed in Sony's 2.x layout, which RPCN also uses.
DW_AUTH_ADDR / DW_LOBBY_ADDR let both servers use port 3074 on two hosts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
